A||N||3||Zorba||Carburated V-8 Installation Questions||||5||
Z||000000||Zorba||10-05-2000||01:37 PM||||V8 set up questions. For those of you who have installed your own carburated v8 engines, replacing a 4 cylinder:<P>1. What do you do with the vapor can and its lines?<P>2. What do you do with the single vacuum line that runs across the brake line, behind the trunk?<P>3. Do the fuel lines have to be moved in any way?<BR>4. What happens to the old junction box by the battery?<BR>5. Why does the right side water heater pipe have to be removed? What does it hit?<BR>6. Is there enough clearance between the right frame rail for a belt change if needed?<BR>7.Are poly bushings necessary to replace the big rear doughnut shaped ones?<BR>8.Is a morosso water electric pump more than adequate if you don't want the W/P drive system in the wheel well?<BR>9. What is the difference between a 4-core radiator for an automatic versus manual?<BR>Are they interchangeable?<BR>10. WHat have you spent on your conversion so far with  a v8 archie kit?<BR>11. Would you get by with a carburated 305-307 until you can afford a 350hp 350 or 383?<BR>Meaning, very noticeable difference after install? There should be significant difference in power and torque.<P>Thank you for any replies for the above questions.||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||10-05-2000||07:05 PM||||The vapor can has 2 line one larger than the other. the large line goes to manifold vacuum the small one goes to Ventury vacuum on the carb.<P>If you have automatic tranny you need to work out a lock method for the torque converter. It helps gas milage considerably on long trips.<P>the dif in radiators is fairly simple. the one for the automatic has a cooler for the tranny in it. manual tranny can use either one but an automatic must have that cooler.||||reg||1
Z||000002||rprevo||10-06-2000||01:12 AM||||I turned my vapor can into a vent for my<BR>gas tank. I hooked my Power brake vacume<BR>line to intake vacume. I have the Morrosso<BR>electric pump and I mounted it in place of the spare tire. When I converted my fathers<BR>88 GT We purchased the Mezier electric water<BR>pump, It beats the Morrosso big time.<BR>I live in Michigan and my car runs about<BR>220 at 70 MPH 3200 RPM With the Mezier<BR>My dads GT dosn't get over 190 The difference<BR>is the Mezier is 35 GPM and the Morrosso is<BR>19 GPM and the Mezier has got a 2000 Hr waranty and there tech support was first class,<BR>  <P>  Ray.<BR>||||reg||6
